{"id": "clm:bf32c1b1e05769266d6be4246d2f4f621c605b313f6ebe4b452a169d2fa3dcbf", "type": "statement", "text": "Debug logging adds resource diffs for PUT/PATCH comparisons and extra Atlas GET requests; MongoDB recommends using debug logging in non-production because it increases load. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/operator/current/ak8so-dry-run.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:9592f033999668500132ae7edc5827674caa4bca8da2fc48b05e2758424cd06b"]}
{"id": "clm:192caa4ebd8bcb189b825581784ff3d0954a97b265d584d88f16233babfdd032", "type": "statement", "text": "Kubernetes API dry run with dryRun=All validates requests without persisting Kubernetes objects. AKO dry run requires actual Kubernetes resources and previews Atlas-side operations, so Kubernetes API validation alone cannot substitute for it. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://kubernetes.io/docs/reference/using-api/api-concepts/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/operator/current/ak8so-dry-run.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:0aa2b64e300e94f57361071ad073756df6d91199b164fd8379f933761366eaf9", "ev:535d90a1db4d0c207dbd5b172048414e7e070fc914775b7a68aa7a51e1fad61b"]}
{"id": "clm:8e698e243b9007dd698b9ef421d70cb1d2bcb617791ffc4e2a304862f3838786", "type": "statement", "text": "AKO dry run performs one reconciliation pass and exits rather than continuously reconciling. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/operator/current/ak8so-dry-run.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/mongodb/mongodb-atlas-kubernetes/v2%40v2.16.0/internal/dryrun"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6d59cf3f38d1945edded7c570fcac26edb9b10d9fe5706467f9897924485975d"]}
{"id": "clm:13987016610c115a47efae7d8c0f32d6f6663658b3cb4113ffde6152c89d5ac9", "type": "statement", "text": "A Kubernetes Job launches AKO with --dry-run. Reconciliation runs once rather than periodically; inspect emitted events with kubectl -n mongodb-atlas-system get events --field-selector reason=DryRun. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/operator/current/ak8so-dry-run.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/mongodb/mongodb-atlas-kubernetes/v2%40v2.16.0/internal/dryrun"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:38878e164e00cbd7b3a0593591f88d38150fd349b36c63e72f54623c3f17448f", "ev:6d59cf3f38d1945edded7c570fcac26edb9b10d9fe5706467f9897924485975d"]}
{"id": "clm:43bd2562cd1c68f08cf9fcfda641de37ac75b5cc536a1b0b9be70b9a3fee57ba", "type": "statement", "text": "Inference from the v2.16.0 transport: a proposed Atlas mutation event does not prove Atlas would accept that request, because the transport returns a local DryRunError instead of sending the mutation. Treat it as an intent preview rather than an end-to-end execution guarantee. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongodb-atlas-kubernetes/blob/v2.16.0/internal/dryrun/transport.go", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/operator/current/ak8so-dry-run.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5f6c763a8905cc98dd44ac7104af9fac1dbfd2e663bc88aac36e2eaf41298d38"]}
{"id": "clm:c25c1a42cc07357a49455c9d202e0138fc0bc9468b7fcdb1941e7857d4371762", "type": "statement", "text": "AKO dry run previews intended Atlas mutations without applying them. In v2.16.0, DryRunTransport forwards GET, CONNECT, TRACE and HEAD requests, but returns DryRunError for other methods; POST, PUT, PATCH and DELETE become proposed create, update or delete messages. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/operator/current/ak8so-dry-run.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongodb-atlas-kubernetes/blob/v2.16.0/internal/dryrun/transport.go"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:5f6c763a8905cc98dd44ac7104af9fac1dbfd2e663bc88aac36e2eaf41298d38", "ev:925ac3884d8c4e3a3b7169601a31dfe8dd38cf3bc272c05c66b3634ccee659b0"]}
{"id": "clm:74977d0f88c57f50bd45b1c521e5ac09104a996ce9e9bcd026f46d589c2df8d5", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB's cached documentation snapshot labels AKO dry run public preview and warns that the feature and documentation may change during preview. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-14)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/operator/current/ak8so-dry-run.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:a412812f9fb0b6d6bd5c3600dc92fcac124511b21e68e96562cc0699d265542d"]}
{"id": "clm:6610808c9b90509c4dc5fa975a0b06f6f1e6304f89ce72f5177129801ed83228", "type": "statement", "text": "For upgrade rehearsals, MongoDB instructs users to use a new Kubernetes/OpenShift cluster with target-version CRDs, custom resources, credential secrets, service account and RBAC. Replacing CRDs on the existing cluster may break reconciliation. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/operator/current/ak8so-dry-run.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f5a6a36d23fd60b1c1cd89144eda743c9e83b61371762050ae3e0fb7f80167e0"]}
{"id": "clm:c01f4ab5e36fd776db63c955b336c0c19513442548ea08b791c532af48167610", "type": "statement", "text": "The Atlas CLI provides atlas kubernetes dry-run, with --operatorVersion, --targetNamespace, --watchNamespace, --watch and --watchTimeout. The documented procedure uses --watch to wait; without it, the CLI exits after installation. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/cli/current/command/atlas-kubernetes-dry-run.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/operator/current/ak8so-dry-run/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:be715da6ba91db1fe13ee65e64a61874c022d5bbdc96c125555dfb1c0641cde3", "ev:c3246714925cb71ab8222a5781607ed203016d41ccaf3e4991ea7d24ca94e071"]}
{"id": "clm:909a112a55ba4b6d08038652560247058b36f034833b974dbbf88b1873a7e03a", "type": "statement", "text": "In release 2.8.1, MongoDB fixed missing dry-run reporting for team-related operations. PR #2268 identifies swallowed errors for AtlasProject team associations; older output could omit intended actions. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongodb-atlas-kubernetes/releases/tag/v2.8.1", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["AKO Dry Run Mode"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/mongodb-atlas-kubernetes/pull/2268"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:f77b5136d3f5cdb20babbf5574ba72a33bee40a2e7ec212f59a1555be723f9fb", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1a47a97514b9e1ad97a8110507cf728d9e343b8ee2cb310f6b3b82d3722df43f", "ev:f410544852dba375c04d0f0960f11427b3cf0d7d58eaf4f58b8f15a1f76ed714"]}
